{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286718-solar-presence-versus-dragon-blooded-presence","id":1286718,"title":"Solar Presence versus Dragon-Blooded Presence","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-11T08:23:10-08:00","id":1286718,"title":"Solar Presence versus Dragon-Blooded Presence","content":"I've heard that the Solar Presence Charm set has more raw power but less actual effectiveness than Terrestrial Presence Charm set.<br /> <br /> How so?<br /> <br /> Does this seem like a real problem to you?<br /> <br /> Would you want to fix this by adding new Solar Presence Charms, or by tweaking or replacing existing Solar Presence Charms?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T10:03:43-08:00","id":1286760,"title":"","content":"I have to say I\u2019m not seeing it. Between Tiger\u2019s Dread Symetry, Harmoneous Presence Meditation, Listener Swaying Argument, and the excellency you\u2019re probably getting a 2m-4m full excellency every time you roll presence. With decent stats in those abilities that just lets you run roughshod all over everyone. DB presence has little tricks to like, double up on giving a persuade and I still action under very specific circumstances, but it can\u2019t compete with throwing 25 dice all day long. Also it has some tricky stuff like mind wiping.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T10:24:09-08:00","id":1286769,"title":"","content":"Let's say I'm Lady Presence McCharisma, the smoothest-talking Solar about.<br /> I want to persuade a guy with a low Resolve (mortal or Exalt) to take a fairly significant action to help me. Should be easy, right?<br /> Well, what I want him to do is a bit risky, quite inconvenient, but it's not very likely he'll die. This requires a major intimacy.<br /> But what if he doesn't have an applicable Major intimacy?<br /> First, I have to give him an applicable minor intimacy. If I succeed, he can resist with 1 wp.<br /> Then I have to give him a second minor intimacy that supports the first one. If I succeed, he can resist with 1 wp.<br /> Then I have to reinforce the first intimacy, using a more significant argument or piece of evidence than the first time.<br /> Then I can finally roll to persuade him. He's got -2 Resolve from the Major Intimacy, so it shouldn't be hard. If he has two other intimacies (one at least Major strength) that oppose my persuasion attempt, he can make a Decision Point (ie spend 1wp).<br /> If I fail any of these, I'll need to change tack entirely, so it's a bit tricky to try again<br /> <br /> Getting lots of successes probably isn't an issue; I'm a Solar presence-monkey after all, his Resolve is rubbish. I've got a huge pool and an excellency.<br /> What I'd like is some way to not have to make 4 different rolls and giving him all these chances to resist with a WP.<br /> <br /> Let's have a look at the Presence tree. What will help me?<br /> Listener-Swaying Argument - No<br /> Harmonious Presence Meditation - No<br /> Excellent Friend Approach - No<br /> Tiger's Dread Symmetry - No<br /> Impassioned Discourse Technique - No<br /> Empowering Shout - No<br /> Majestic Radiant Presence - No<br /> Underling-Promoting Touch - No<br /> Threefold Magnetic Ardor - No<br /> Awakened Carnal Demiurge - No<br /> Enemy-Castigating Judgement - No<br /> Fulminating Word - Will make the final intimidation/persuasion cost 2 wp instead of 1! But costs 1wp. And he could just spend WP to not get the intimacy in the first place.<br /> Authority-Radiating Stance - No<br /> Terrifying Apparition of Glory - I can't use it unless my anima is at bonfire, and then the Wyld Hunt would know where I am.<br /> Blazing Glorious Icon - No<br /> Mind-Wiping Gaze - No<br /> Hypnotic Tongue Technique - Perfect! No problem! Sorted! As long as you're cool with hypnotising people.<br /> Worshipful Lackey Acquisition - No<br /> Prophet-Uplifting Prana - No<br /> Shedding Infinite Radiance - No<br /> Rose Lipped Seduction Style - No<br /> Crowned King of Eternity - No<br /> Favor-Conferring Prana - No<br /> Countenance of Vast Wrath - I can't use it unless my anima is iconic, and then the Wyld Hunt would know where I am.<br /> <br /> Solar Presence only has one charm that's useful for getting past the lack of intimacies, and that's Hypnotic Tongue. But you can't really use that when, say, trying to convince a Queen to help you in her court, because her guards will attack you.<br /> <br /> Essentially, Solar Presence charms do four main things well:<br /> Buff your friends<br /> Help you get lots of successes for cheap<br /> Help you intimidate people<br /> Help you seduce people<br /> <br /> None of those let you deal with the difficulty of persuading people to take significant actions when they don't already have a Major intimacy. And if they already did have a Major intimacy? There's a decent chance you wouldn't need to Persuade them anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T10:26:47-08:00","id":1286773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286718-solar-presence-versus-dragon-blooded-presence?p=1286760#post1286760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">throwing 25 dice all day long.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> lets you run roughshod all over everyone. </div> </div> </div>The problem is, the first one does not necessarily lead to the second one.<br /> <br /> Our Zenith preacher regularly rolls 15+ successes.<br /> <br /> He's had so little success at getting people to do what he wants that he fell into suicidal depression.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T10:34:19-08:00","id":1286777,"title":"","content":"Okay, so Lady Presence McCharisma was taking ages to try and persuade the weak-willed King to ally with her nation.<br /> <br /> Now it's time for Cynis Silver Tongue to take her turn.<br /> <br /> How could she give him a major intimacy? Minor, 2nd minor, reinforce to Major?<br /> <br /> Nah, she just throws down Dragon Warlord's Convocation. She immediately rolls to give him a Major Intimacy of loyalty to her. He'd like to spend a WP... but he can only do that if he has two intimacies, one being Major, that oppose this. And then she can move on to Persuading him. Four rolls turned into two.<br /> <br /> (Alternatively, she could first roll to give him a Minor intimacy of loyalty to her. If it doesn't work, go to Dragon Warlord's Convocation. If it does, then Dragon Warlord's Convocation will give him a Defining Intimacy, and to resist with WP he'd need two intimacies that oppose it, one being Defining.)<br /> <br /> That is once/story... but Solars don't have anything like that.<br /> <br /> That's not the only charm that helps with Persuasion; there are charms that mean the target can count less intimacies when trying to find the two to apply to a Decision Point (really good), charms where the target counts as already having a supporting intimacy, etc.<br /> And they have a lot of good charms for Inspiring emotions and doing stuff with emotions.<br /> <br /> They're not as good at intimidation or seduction though. Or just getting loads of successes without spending many motes.<br /> (Of course, for DBs flaring during a conversation is less problematic than for a Solar, though still awkward.)<br /> <br /> If I was playing a Dragonblood in a Solar game, and looking for stuff I could do that they couldn't, I might well go for Presence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-11-2019, 01:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T11:25:34-08:00","id":1286793,"title":"","content":"I could have sworn there were some Solar presence charms that effectively give the target the same intimacies you hold. But maybe they just give you more dice if that\u2019s the case?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T11:25:49-08:00","id":1286794,"title":"","content":"Would it be best for a Solar to have some way to break through the normal social influence system's protections by playing to their strength of overwhelming force?<br /> <br /> Like, if you score enough threshold successes, you can achieve an effect like Warlord's Convocation... but you need to score enough threshold successes, so anyone strong enough to not get overwhelmed still has a defense against you.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T11:31:30-08:00","id":1286796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286718-solar-presence-versus-dragon-blooded-presence?p=1286769#post1286769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">None of those let you deal with the difficulty of persuading people to take significant actions when they don't already have a Major intimacy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that Solar Presence is in a good position of having a lot of good glorious or fearsome god-king imagery to draw on to give it a lot to do, without being something that trivialises the agendas or personalities of other people.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if they already did have a Major intimacy? There's a decent chance you wouldn't need to Persuade them anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that's really consistent with the intent of the social system, or necessarily tracks logically. A person having a Major Principle of opposition to the Realm doesn't automatically incline them towards doing so on your terms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T11:35:55-08:00","id":1286797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286718-solar-presence-versus-dragon-blooded-presence?p=1286769#post1286769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Getting lots of successes probably isn't an issue; I'm a Solar presence-monkey after all, his Resolve is rubbish. I've got a huge pool and an excellency.<br /> What I'd like is some way to not have to make 4 different rolls and giving him all these chances to resist with a WP.</div> </div> </div> </div>Put another way, unless I'm misreading the situation as you describe, Solars are strong <i>but</i> depend a lot on ST discretion about whether X NPC would spend a WP or not, ranging from &quot;Of course he would!&quot; to &quot;Why would he? What reason / feeling does he have that makes him?&quot;. And I guess they do not have anything in other Abilities to much help with this? (Consideration because Solars get a hell of a lot of Favoured Abilities, choice in their Caste Abilities and are parts of Circles).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T11:41:58-08:00","id":1286798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286718-solar-presence-versus-dragon-blooded-presence?p=1286777#post1286777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Of course, for DBs flaring during a conversation is less problematic than for a Solar, though still awkward.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't flaring in a conversation literally start harming those you're talking to and/or your surroundings? Even if the king/queen is up on a raised dais and you're down on the floor petitioning them, I doubt they'll appreciate you suddenly wrecking their throne room.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T11:57:24-08:00","id":1286801,"title":"","content":"Also, the solar intimidation charms are like nukes, like Terrifying Apparition of Glory. You use them in combat, combat more or less ends (or the targets pay the not inconsiderate 1wp and 5 init cost, and the charm is useless), and that can take a whole lot of fun from combat players. Also, the charm recurs again, and again. My players that have the tacit understanding of not overusing it, but in my opinion it could be better designed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T12:16:12-08:00","id":1286807,"title":"","content":"Oh right, Warlord\u2019s Convocation. I literally didn\u2019t even re-read that one because I looked at the essence requirement and went \u201cwell that\u2019s barely worth considering for a splat without Supernals.\u201d I suppose in that one case the DBs are better, but it\u2019s only once per story and leaves you with a possibly undesireable track back to you. The later is a minor downside, for sure.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m also not sure I\u2019m understanding the social system properly. Doesn\u2019t that description describe the absolute worst case scenario, where you don\u2019t know any of your target\u2019s intimacies, a few strong ones can directly oppose what you want, and they\u2019re willing to enter decision points at the drop of a hat?<br /> <br /> It was my impression that if you wanted, for instance, somebody to run off and join your army to fight the Realm, that first you acertain that they have a defining intimacy of \u201cMy family is everything.\u201d And then you target that by saying \u201cThe Realm isn\u2019t here today, it won\u2019t be here tomorrow, but it\u2019s coming, and when it does your family will be slaves forever. Come with me, and save them before they ever get hurt.\u201d That way not only can they not bring their \u201cMy family is everything.\u201d Intimacy to bear to defend, since you used it to attack, but they need two OTHER ones that are just as strong.<br /> <br /> To persuade somebody to do something you don\u2019t need an intimacy that absolutely fully supports it, there\u2019d be almost no point to the social system if it did. You just can\u2019t say something with no logical connection like \u201cYou love your family, I am hungry, therefore make me a sandwich.\u201d Unless it\u2019s a threat I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T12:56:28-08:00","id":1286817,"title":"","content":"Oh, this is something I meant to bring up in another thread but just realized I forgot to ever do so<br /> <br /> I find solar presence a bit odd specifically in comparison to the other social abilities. I would have thought presence is the upfront power ability, socialize handles guile, read intentions, and handles social stuff in the larger contexts of society, and then performance has the more weird affects like memory rewriting. But it seems like socialize has most of the good mechanical social influence affects in addition to it's intimacy stuff. Indecent proposal method sounds more presence to me, having the charisma and speaking skills to make bad ideas sound sensible, and given it doesn't really interact with specific contexts I don't see why it's socialize, and effective counter argument looks the same way. And all the socialize affects in miricales (save viper scenting method) look like they'd work better in presence too. ESPECIALLY soul testing method, reaching to someone based on personal magnetism from a shared experience is squarely presence, if socialize encompasses all affects that have to do with interpersonal relationships then that would be every social affect ever<br /> <br /> This would be alright if presence had its own share of social tricks to match, but it doesn't. It has a select number of power boosters and then the majority of the rest are the buff charms that don't relate to actually influencing someone, and then small branches for seduction threaten specificay. To be frank it seems like the old devs got presence and socialize confused with charisma and manipulation, like presence is only ever allowed to be the most straight forward affects possible when it also applies to lying and deceit just as well<br /> <br /> Though this might be because I'm a nut for social systems and powers in general, who knows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3109,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3109-lionmanguy","user":"Lionmanguy","date":". 02-11-2019, 04:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3109-lionmanguy","name":"Lionmanguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T15:43:44-08:00","id":1286876,"title":"","content":"Well, that's the post I've had the most direct quotes from ever.<br /> I'm glad I'm giving you guys something to debate. In the last week I feel like this forum has come alive again, which is great as Lunars is going to hit tomorrow.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286718-solar-presence-versus-dragon-blooded-presence?p=1286793#post1286793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could have sworn there were some Solar presence charms that effectively give the target the same intimacies you hold. But maybe they just give you more dice if that\u2019s the case?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're thinking of Impassioned Discourse technique. That cuts the cost of an excellency when you try and persuade someone to do something that you have a Principle in support of.<br /> <br /> For example, if you try and convince someone to fight the Realm, and you have a Defining intimacy of &quot;The Realm must be defeated&quot;, you get +1 success and +4 dice for only 3m.<br /> <br /> (Obviously, like a lot of the Presence charms at the bottom of the tree, it claims it gives you extra dice. But it doesn't, it turns 2 dice into a success and then makes excellencies cheaper. Or... sometimes more expensive if you use it without thinking. This is something that took my players quite a while to get the hang of. I had to remind them a lot.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Put another way, unless I'm misreading the situation as you describe, Solars are strong <i>but</i> depend a lot on ST discretion about whether X NPC would spend a WP or not, ranging from &quot;Of course he would!&quot; to &quot;Why would he? What reason / feeling does he have that makes him?&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually it wasn't, though that's a good point too.<br /> <br /> Basically, there's two issues with Persuasion.<br /> 1) Your target needs to have an applicable intimacy.<br /> 2) They can spend WP to bounce it off (at various stages; the Persuasion is the hardest to spend WP).<br /> <br /> Dragonblood have various charms that help with both 1) and 2).<br /> <br /> Solars have nothing in Presence that helps with the 1). They have one charm that helps with 2), a bit, but it's expensive. (Fulminating Word costs you 1wp, and means your Persuasion attempt needs to be resisted with 2wp, rather than 1. But it doesn't stop them spending WP to not get an intimacy. So useful but expensive if you've solved Problem 1 and need to solve Problem 2)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I guess they do not have anything in other Abilities to much help with this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not the WP, no. But for 1, see my reply to Lionmanguy at the bottom of this post.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Even if the king/queen is up on a raised dais and you're down on the floor petitioning them, I doubt they'll appreciate you suddenly wrecking their throne room.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I said it's still awkward. Less awkward than revealing you're an ancient body-stealing demon of course.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">(or the targets pay the not inconsiderate 1wp and 5 init cost, and the charm is useless)</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, while &quot;useless&quot;, I think 7m, 1wp is worth it to burn off 1wp and 5 initiative from each of your foes. Or even one foe.<br /> <br /> As I said, Solar Presence is quite good at intimidation (and seduction).<br /> It's just not good at Persuasion (or Inspiration, I think. I'd need to check).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh right, Warlord\u2019s Convocation. I literally didn\u2019t even re-read that one because I looked at the essence requirement and went \u201cwell that\u2019s barely worth considering for a splat without Supernals.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>With 25000 Dragonblood in the world, some of whom are hundreds of years, I'm sure there's more Dragonblood with Presence 5 and Essence 4+ than there are Solars with Presence 1+ and Essence 1+. Probably a fair few more.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I suppose in that one case the DBs are better, but it\u2019s only once per story </div> </div> </div>It is.<br /> But Solars can't even do that once a year.<br /> <br /> I used Warlord's Convocation because it's their best Presence charm, but they have a number of other charms that a Solar who wants to make Persuasion attempts would find more useful than most of her own charms. I just don't have time to go through them.<br /> (I may do it tomorrow evening or Wednesday morning if I have time.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m also not sure I\u2019m understanding the social system properly. Doesn\u2019t that description describe the absolute worst case scenario, where you don\u2019t know any of your target\u2019s intimacies</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but that's going to happen most of the time you're talking to people you don't know well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">a few strong ones can directly oppose what you want,</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, again my example didn't say if they definitely did, just that they might.<br /> It's harder if they do, because they can use a Decision Point.<br /> <br /> If they have no opposing intimacies, that's easier, because they can't use a Decision Point. But you still need them to have a supporting intimacy, and if they don't, it's quite hard to give them one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">and they\u2019re willing to enter decision points at the drop of a hat?</div> </div> </div> </div>I used a Major decision for an example, because I think it might be a big enough ask that they'll want to spend 1wp to resist.<br /> But they won't always. As I said, it's an option, not a certainty.<br /> But if, say, you're trying to convince a Queen to ally her nation with yours, that seems like something she might rather spend a WP than do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was my impression that if you wanted, for instance, somebody to run off and join your army to fight the Realm, that first you acertain that they have a defining intimacy of \u201cMy family is everything.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>But how do you ascertain that?<br /> (See my reply at the bottom here, to Lionmanguy)<br /> <br /> And what if... well, you want them to do something, and they just don't have any Major or Defining intimacies that are applicable?<br /> That's been an issue for our social characters a fair few times.<br /> <br /> As you said, my example is... somewhat of a worst possible example.<br /> But it's a situation that I've seen come up a lot of times.<br /> <br /> Whereas your example, is the best possible example (you realise they have a Defining Intimacy that's useful). I've used that once.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">To persuade somebody to do something you don\u2019t need an intimacy that absolutely fully supports it, there\u2019d be almost no point to the social system if it did.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, but that's not really what I'm saying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lionmanguy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it seems like socialize has most of the good mechanical social influence affects in addition to it's intimacy stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are powerful social influence effects in Presence.<br /> It's great at hypnotising, intimidation, and seduction. It's also good at getting past high Resolve without spending a ton of motes (which is very dull, but sometimes necessary).<br /> <br /> What it's not good at is Persuasion (or Inspire).<br /> <br /> It can get lots of successes.<br /> But what it can't do is a)tell you what intimacies people have so you can key off them, and b)if they don't have useful intimacies make it easier for you to give people intimacies that you can then key off.<br /> <br /> But there are effects for this; they're in Socialise. The very first charm of Socialise, for example, makes anyone with a positive intimacy to their culture have a temporary minor positive intimacy to you. And they can't spend WP to resist! That's incredibly useful! Once they've got a Minor Intimacy to you, you could use it for all kinds of shenanigans on their other intimacies.*<br /> The second charm listed is a dice boost to Read Intentions, but if you repurchase it, it becomes a really good charm for learning your target's intimacies. Very important for social influence!<br /> <br /> *This is pretty much the only Solar charm that does this. Dragonblood have a bunch.<br /> <br /> And of course, Wise-Eyed Courtier Method will let you walk into a social group and immediately learn a ton of useful intimacies and emotions.<br /> <br /> So, you see, Presence is bad at Persuasion. But it can be good, if you combine it with a bunch of Socialise charms.<br /> <br /> But, unfortunately, the Zenith player in our game didn't realise that. He took a lot of Presence and Persuasion charms, and well... he's great at preaching to the converted. Literally. What he's not great at is convincing the people who don't much like us to get on better with us, which is what we desperately need.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-11-2019, 07:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T16:01:53-08:00","id":1286880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286718-solar-presence-versus-dragon-blooded-presence?p=1286796#post1286796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that Solar Presence is in a good position of having a lot of good glorious or fearsome god-king imagery to draw on to give it a lot to do, without being something that trivialises the agendas or personalities of other people.</div> </div> </div> </div>I quoted this seperarely, because I think it's worth discussing in a different way to the stuff above.<br /> <br /> Solars have nothing beyond more dice to help them with the fact that, if someone just doesn't care about helping the poor, you probably can't convince them to help the poor.<br /> <br /> And... should they?<br /> <br /> When our ST read the new social system, he was very happy. &quot;A Solar can't just walk up to a stranger and convince them to join their army anymore! That's great! It's much more realistic.&quot;<br /> And it is.<br /> <br /> And I don't think (except for straight-up mind-control, like Hypnotic Tongue Technique) that a Solar should be able to, say, convince people to take Serious Tasks when they don't have a Major intimacy that supports it.<br /> <br /> I mean, it doesn't really make sense for a Solar to just walk up to someone and be like &quot;abandon your old life and become my follower!&quot; and it work. Who'd do that?*<br /> <br /> *I guess Jesus's disciples (he is an inspiration for Zeniths). But then they probably had Major Intimacies like &quot;YHWH will send us a Messiah and we should follow him&quot; or maybe &quot;I want to give my life more meaning than being a fisherman&quot;. Not to mention &quot;I'll do whatever it takes to drive out the Romans.&quot; Oh St Simon, you wacky terrorist, you.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> At the beginning of this thread, Sunder asked if anyone had any ideas for how Solar Presence could be improved.<br /> <br /> In terms of Persuasion, I wouldn't suggest things like &quot;Make a Persuasion attempt without needing a supporting intimacy.&quot;<br /> <br /> But instead, I'd suggest things like:<br /> Make it harder for them to apply a Decision Point<br /> Increase the cost of resisting a new intimacy or having an intimacy degraded.<br /> Increase a Minor intimacy to Major without a second intimacy supporting it.<br /> Instill a Major intimacy with a successful instill, rather than a Minor. (Should be expensive.)<br /> Persuade them to do a Serious Task with a Minor intimacy, or a Life-Threatening Task with a Major Intimacy. (Should be expensive.)<br /> Have your target count as having certain Minor Intimacies under certain circumstances (like Mastery of Small Manners. There's a fair few Dragonblood charms that do this.)<br /> <br /> Some of these wouldn't be general, but be Solar themed. Ie you can't instill any Major Intimacy, but only Principles based on morality or honour. Or maybe there's a charm that means they can't apply negative Ties (of hatred, etc) to a Decision Point. Or you can persuade them to do a Serious Task with a Minor intimacy, but it has to be protecting people. Or you can reduce a Negative minor tie to nothing with no WP to resist, but only negative intimacies to you.<br /> I'm sure people could think of some ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-11-2019, 07:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T16:09:23-08:00","id":1286886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286718-solar-presence-versus-dragon-blooded-presence?p=1286876#post1286876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With 25000 Dragonblood in the world, some of whom are hundreds of years, I'm sure there's more Dragonblood with Presence 5 and Essence 4+ than there are Solars with Presence 1+ and Essence 1+. Probably a fair few more.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Of course, this knowledge is cold comfort to me when I have to wait <b>52 sessions</b> (!) before I can even pick up the Charm, much less start thinking about using it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T16:11:45-08:00","id":1286888,"title":"","content":"Incidentally, I'd be happy to hear from anyone who's used a Solar with Presence charms.<br /> <br /> I've found them not much good unless they're also good at Socialise, but I'd like to see others' experience.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T16:15:47-08:00","id":1286890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286718-solar-presence-versus-dragon-blooded-presence?p=1286886#post1286886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Of course, this knowledge is cold comfort to me when I have to wait <b>52 sessions</b> (!) before I can even pick up the Charm, much less start thinking about using it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, okay sure, but it is the absolute top of Dragonblood Presence.<br /> <br /> (Every Dragonblood PC I've played or played alongside has had Essence 4 since... oh, I'm going to say about 8 years ago. So I realise this is a bigger thing for others.)<br /> <br /> I'm not comparing a DB with it to a random Solar, I'm comparing it to a high-Essence Solar. Or Presence Supernal Solar.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T16:38:30-08:00","id":1286894,"title":"","content":"Wizard, you're right in that Socialize is better at determining Intimacies than Presence. That's its job. (And protecting your own, of course.) Even if the Zenith in your group didn't take Socialize, are you telling me that <i>no one</i> in your group took Socialize? I mean, yeah, of course you're going to have problems with social influence if your <i>group</i> has no way of determining Intimacies.<br /> <br /> I think you harp on this too much, frankly. If anything, the DB has misplaced Charms, not Solars. Presence shouldn't be about 'getting Intimacies', as that is the purview of Socialize. Also, I'd have to question any ST that would allow a social-focused character to that degree to make that sort of mistake. That's like taking Archery Supernal, and not taking Dodge, Resistance, or any other way to defend yourself. You're missing a vital part of the Social system if you can't determine Intimacies.<br /> <br /> Also, something else that should be noted here--and likely any ST Guide that is created--is that NPC Intimacies <i>should</i> exist at <i>some</i> level to support social interaction. I'm not saying make it easy; I'm not saying to make it simple. There is some onus on the ST to not completely block the Social system by saying, 'Yeah, no, none of these guys have <i>any</i> Intimacies that can help.' If the ST gives them Intimacies, but the Solars can't figure out how to exploit them, then the Solars fail. But if there are no handles, the ST has failed. There's also the fact that Social system is far more of a detective game or puzzle than the Combat system in Exalted 3E, and people wanting to circumvent it to make it more like Combat I think are short-changing the system.<br /> <br /> I just don't see the problem. From a 'stereotypical' Solar Circle POV, the Eclipse finds the right target, and the Zenith persuades that target.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3551-ulthwithian","name":"Ulthwithian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T16:39:31-08:00","id":1286895,"title":"","content":"If people want to see some other examples of the kinds of charms that would be useful for a silver-tongued Solar, look at the previewed charms Uncertain Sky Ambiguity and Herd-Reinforcement Stance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T16:54:25-08:00","id":1286902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286718-solar-presence-versus-dragon-blooded-presence?p=1286777#post1286777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Of course, for DBs flaring during a conversation is less problematic than for a Solar, though still awkward.)<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Incidentally, I personally had a hard time effectively conceptualising anima banners or other aura effects in such settings before I saw Kill la Kill.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.dailymotion.com/video/x3cvvno\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.dailymotion.com/video/x3cvvno\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.dailymotion.com/video/x3cvvno\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.dailymotion.com/video/x3cvvno </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T17:02:34-08:00","id":1286904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286718-solar-presence-versus-dragon-blooded-presence?p=1286888#post1286888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidentally, I'd be happy to hear from anyone who's used a Solar with Presence charms.<br /> <br /> I've found them not much good unless they're also good at Socialise, but I'd like to see others' experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm playing a Solar with Presence Charms, but he's also Socialize Supernal.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat said, I don't feel that investment into Socialize represents some sort of error in the design of Solar Presence - the hole is <i>supposed</i> to be there. Not every Ability can be Melee, nor should it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T17:07:13-08:00","id":1286906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286718-solar-presence-versus-dragon-blooded-presence?p=1286876#post1286876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What it's not good at is Persuasion (or Inspire).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, and that's my main problem. The other stuff about intimacies I fully get, read intentions is a socialize based roll so obviously it's going to have all the read intentions charms, I don't want any of those in presence. What I'm asking is why, once you know what the person's intimacies are or just decide to brute force your way through it by instilling multiple intimacies and chaining them upwards on their won, all the cool tricks related to the persuade action are in socialize. Presence is supposed to be the straightforward raw talky skill ability, it should be able to do stuff like that, and some of those tricks don't really make sense to me as specifically socialize related. I mean don't get me wrong this isn't a huge complaint or anything, it's more me being weird about this one section of the system I'm obsessive over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3109-lionmanguy","name":"Lionmanguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T17:38:45-08:00","id":1286913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286718-solar-presence-versus-dragon-blooded-presence?p=1286888#post1286888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidentally, I'd be happy to hear from anyone who's used a Solar with Presence charms.<br /> <br /> I've found them not much good unless they're also good at Socialise, but I'd like to see others' experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>I played a Solar with moderate-heavy investment in Presence and Performance and minimal (ie. not even the excellency) Socialize. I expected a lot of trouble going in because of the lack of Socialize than I actually experienced. Just talking to NPCs for a while or observing them for a scene or two was enough to give a rough idea of at least one intimacy to work with so I could usually target something blind with good odds. And if that failed (or was resisted) following up with an Inspire and then playing off that emotion usually did the trick as well. You're not wrong that it takes more rolls, but it was effective enough to wear down erode the faith of an Immaculate monk before Essence 3 with no social abilities Supernal.<br /> <br /> It was also worth its weight in gold during combat. Harmonious Presence Methodology + Poised Lion Attitude meant that I could fire off a simple social action with 11 dice every round in addition to normal combat actions for 3m. They didn't all land, but as combat drags on Willpower and motes for Resolve become increasingly scarce. Enemies could choose between being Inspired with anger and easily manipulated/Instilled with some less than ideal feelings, or they could burn willpower they would rather spend on charms to resist.<br /> <br /> By the time we finished at Essence 3 I was also running around with Sun King Radiance from Integrity, so anyone already broken (or any new allies watching for the first time) sad, at the ST's option, the ability to manifest a new Major Intimacy of respect with nearly every social pass my idealistic Eclipse made.<br /> <br /> Socialize would have made the build frighteningly more powerful, but it never felt particularly weak or ineffective in the social arena despite the gaping blind spot. But I also went into things knowing that blind spot would be there and prepared for what it would mean for how effective he could be and how I would need to approach things. If I hadn't gone in with open eyes I can imagine that it would have been deeply frustrating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12145-arion-wind","name":"Arion Wind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T18:31:59-08:00","id":1286926,"title":"","content":"I guess my feeling has always been that Solar Presence should be good at 1) being glorious and 2) convincing others of the rightness of your cause. From this thread it sounds like it does pretty well at the first one, but falls down a bit at 2. Honestly, I could see Solar Presence having a charm which allows you to treat someone as having a minor intimacy towards one of your defining intimacies, because your charisma and enthusiasm for your subject leaks over into your target. Or a charm which lets you get away with instilling one of your own defining intimacies into your target with only one supporting intimacy. <br /> <br /> Basically, I think Wizard's earlier suggestions mostly work, but I'd tend to require them to reflect the Solar's own defining intimacies and maybe have them fall down a bit if an opponent is really dead set against you, on the basis that Zeniths get to define their own definition of &quot;Righteousness&quot; in 3e, instead of applying some version of the Sun's definition of it. This way, it works for getting followers to your cause and getting your flock to do things for you, but trying to convince people to do things you wouldn't do or things that are tangential to your main goals, is where Socialize can really help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T18:37:42-08:00","id":1286927,"title":"","content":"I think that might be why socialize seems more powerful than perhaps it should be. With my experience in the system nobody used socialize to figure out that the sneering Satrap who treated his servants like David Lynch\u2019s Baron Vladimir Harkonen had an intimacy of contempt for the local people. Where socialize is useful is to find out that he actually doesn\u2019t and it\u2019s all a show, or that he secretly loves one of them or something.<br /> <br /> It happens enough to still be useful, especially in really high class socialite settings where you can pretty much assume everyone is hiding something, but a whole lot of the time you can just guess based on actions, or speech. Like if you come across a guy, respected in his community, good person to try and get on your side, and he lives out on the edge of the forest, keeping it clear of deadfall and making sure it isn\u2019t over hunted. Tell him the Realm is coming to slash and burn down this whole forest to get at your circle, and no, it won\u2019t matter if you\u2019ve already skipped town because they\u2019ll do it anyway just to be sure. You\u2019re not 100% sure he\u2019s got an intimacy towards the woods, but he probably does.<br /> <br /> Presence could definitely do with a treatment for having more cool punchy effects, but also when you\u2019re playing a Solar some of that has to come from you too. Like you don\u2019t have a lot of cool feats of strength charms, but picking up a giant beer still and dousing a flaming house is more about how you applied your 30 dice double 7s.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 02-11-2019, 09:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T19:35:51-08:00","id":1286950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286718-solar-presence-versus-dragon-blooded-presence?p=1286888#post1286888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidentally, I'd be happy to hear from anyone who's used a Solar with Presence charms.<br /> <br /> I've found them not much good unless they're also good at Socialise, but I'd like to see others' experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't necessarily need to know the targets intimacy. Minor intimacies can be put in on their own without any other, and then used to chain up higher, or build a pyramid of sorts of related intimacies. Yeah that takes a while but it totally works, and hell sometimes it will be necessary even with socialize, if the character in question has intimacies that are just all bad and opposed to what you want to get to. The problem isn't viability at all, because that totally works. Its just the slightest bit boring is all I was getting at.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3109-lionmanguy","name":"Lionmanguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T23:16:29-08:00","id":1286983,"title":"","content":"I don't have time to go into what people have said, because I have got to go to work.<br /> <br /> But I will just say:<br /> A) Some people have said that I'm kind of making this too hard: you should use Socialise to find out their intimacies, and chances are they have a related major or defining intimacy, and not two opposed intimacies of required strength.<br /> In that case... Why do you need Presence charms? Your excellency will be enough.<br /> Presence charms aren't for easy situations, they're for hard ones.<br /> <br /> 2)Yeah, Poised Lion is great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T01:01:44-08:00","id":1286991,"title":"","content":"It's been pointed out to me, and reading the charm again I agree, that Impassioned Discourse Technique allows the solar to leverage their own intimacies as if they were the target's:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ex3 p370</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">[...] In essence, this Charm persuades a character to act as the Solar would act. She might argue from her own compassionate principles to convince her target to be merciful or generous, or principles reflecting temperance, to convince the target to abstain from debauchery, vice, dereliction or iniquity. Likewise she might invoke valorous Intimacies to urge courageous action, or she might sell a course of action with the force of her conviction.</div> </div> </div> </div>While the first part sounds mostly like fluff, the last sentence makes the context pretty clear to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8977-sigfriedmcwild","name":"sigfriedmcwild","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8977_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T01:11:31-08:00","id":1286993,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s kind of amusing seeing this thread because the very first or second time I read Solar Presence I thought \u201cYou know what this tree really needs? A Charm to instill a new Tie at Major intensity.\u201d I\u2019ve been forgetting to write one ever since.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sigfriedmcwild</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286718-solar-presence-versus-dragon-blooded-presence?p=1286991#post1286991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's been pointed out to me, and reading the charm again I agree, that Impassioned Discourse Technique allows the solar to leverage their own intimacies as if they were the target's:<br /> <br /> While the first part sounds mostly like fluff, the last sentence makes the context pretty clear to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, those are all just descriptions of the Solar arguing in favor of her own Intimacies, which is the thing the Charm is for doing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T04:21:28-08:00","id":1287017,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's just fluff.<br /> <br /> A charm that let you count the target as having your intimacies would be very OP, even at Essence 5, let alone Essence 1.<br /> You could make Pelleps Delled attack the Wyld Hunt because you have a Defining Intimacy of &quot;The Realm is evil.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T04:56:25-08:00","id":1287020,"title":"","content":"Wiz, I find it amazing you're consistently portraying a view of the social system diametrically opposed to mine. Dragon Warlord's Convocation is exactly the kind of design I fear going forwards, just dumping random high level intimacies on people while barely engaging with the system, it feels much the same as if it was a melee charm that said &quot;roll against DV, if you pass then opponents hand just came off&quot;.<br /> And as for then Zenith in your game, you know he's been iffy with the social combat not due to not having the resources on his sheet but because he's used to 2nd ed social combat and is still adjusting to the differences, surely?<br /> <br /> And I don't think socialise is especially required, although I certainly wouldn't deny it is very helpful, most people give away at least a couple of intimacies they hold just by how they act normally, and that plus popping a minor or two on someone is fine as a launching platform.<br /> <br /> As a counterpoint in general, Solar Presence in 3e has got me buying into it as a non-social focused character for the first time in Exalted ever so ultimately I find it far more evocative and engaging than previous editions, whereas Dragonblood Presence gets largely a big 'meh' with a sideline of grumbling from me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25050-fodor","name":"FODOR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T04:59:05-08:00","id":1287481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286718-solar-presence-versus-dragon-blooded-presence#post1286718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does this seem like a real problem to you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mixed feelings.<br /> I'm pretty okay with the idea that the esoteric powers of the other Exalts are (in their limited ways) better at ignoring someone's preferences and bending them to your will. However, Dragon Warlord's Convocation is very much presented as &quot;my awesome presence demands your loyalty!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T06:07:59-08:00","id":1287506,"title":"","content":"It definitely seems like if Dragon-Blooded can speed up the steps from 4 to 2 at least once per story, Solars should too. <br /> <br /> \u201cConvince you of the rightness of my cause!\u201d And all that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T12:58:17-08:00","id":1287639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286718-solar-presence-versus-dragon-blooded-presence?p=1286876#post1286876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">snip<br /> But, unfortunately, the Zenith player in our game didn't realise that. He took a lot of Presence and Persuasion charms, and well... he's great at preaching to the converted. Literally. What he's not great at is convincing the people who don't much like us to get on better with us, which is what we desperately need.</div> </div> </div> </div>This has been a problem in my game. The Zenith is really good at scaring enemies into not attacking, but can't convince worth beans. It probably doesn't help that players all know they can chuck two handfuls of dice at things leading them to expect success through raw power. Combine that with the often time-sensitive nature of plot and they don't usually attempt to figure out NPC intimacies or instill and upgrade new ones.<br /> <br /> I find it odd that persuade is worded such that physical actions, not information gathering through conversation is what it governs, but in the absence of any other 'how do you get someone to tell you something' mechanics I've been using it as information gathering as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/977-major","name":"Major","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar977_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T16:16:30-08:00","id":1287733,"title":"","content":"Re; topic in the thread where, to paraphrase, other Exalted can be OKd to have social powers Solars don't, because other Exalted have powers more suited to bending or ignoring others preferences, my feeling on this is it really depends on the Exalt type Solars are being compared to.<br /> <br /> Like, I think anything that is acceptable for a Dragonblood should be acceptable for a Solar because, to my mind, other you can make a system statement that Dragonblood essence lends itself more to coercing people against their will than Solar. To my mind, that really does not fit with or constructively add to the dynamic between the two splats, and its really quite a bad statement to add there.<br /> <br /> Likewise really for Sidereals and Lunars, although I think it's more acceptable given how their patrons work and the kind of magic their themes and feel promise.<br /> <br /> On the other hand of course, it's pretty clearly OK for Abyssals and Infernals and really some of the stranger 3e splats (Hearteaters) to have this property.<br /> <br /> The more important thing of course, rather than splat dynamics and themes, is to complement, rather than obviate, the richness going on in the standard social game though! Even for splats that are relatively &quot;Mind Control OK&quot;, diabolical cleverness can be cooler to play with that brute force.<br /> <br /> (Edit: If it helps at all to explain, when you pick up a Dragonblooded, you do so to be a elemental warrior, or a Sidereal to be a subtle genius of the stars, or a Lunar to be an flexible shapeshifter. Those are your core pitch for those character types.<br /> <br /> That doesn't come with the expectation that your Charms should be violating in a way that the shiny Solar Exalted's are not, and it's probably mostly unwanted for you to be told that they are, if my intuitions and expectations are much like the typical ones.<br /> <br /> But when you play an Infernal or Abyssal or similar, you are probably coming in from a point of view where you expect and are mostly cool with being somewhat inherently a thing that violates mortal will. YMMV tho.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":929,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","user":"Ghosthead","date":". 02-13-2019, 07:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T07:34:05-08:00","id":1287933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286718-solar-presence-versus-dragon-blooded-presence?p=1287733#post1287733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, I think anything that is acceptable for a Dragonblood should be acceptable for a Solar because, to my mind, other you can make a system statement that Dragonblood essence lends itself more to coercing people against their will than Solar. To my mind, that really does not fit with or constructively add to the dynamic between the two splats, and its really quite a bad statement to add there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Historically Dragon-Blooded have had a couple of pretty esoteric powers, for example in 1st and 2nd edition a side effect of Bestow the Saffron Mantle allowed a dead Dragon-Blooded bureaucrat to hijack the body of their proxy and get revenge from beyond the grave before their soul was forced to move on. A potentially confusing statement about Dragon-Blooded charms but its existence made for a worthwhile plothook.<br /> They've gotten less weird in Ex3 when surcharge and element segregation went away, that was a major cause of why (for example) half of performance used to be dedicated to being a sneaky musical assassin due to a forray into larceny or stealth being punished.<br /> <br /> But I digress, There's ways I could've been sold on Dragon-Blooded mind control.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 02-14-2019, 12:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T08:04:18-08:00","id":1287942,"title":"","content":"I'm not so sure. The core <i>weakness</i> in the Solar Charmset that I think is often overlooked is that, relative to other Exalts, their Core Charm Identity (CCI) is excellence. This means that they should be the most efficient/powerful at being excellent. This is generally translated as 'more successes', and not 'cool new things you can do with your Essence'. So the issue in this thread is, apparently, this weakness is being exposed. Other Exalts generally have a CCI that makes it easier/more likely to have 'cool things with Essence' rather than 'more successes'. The DBs are an excellent example of this, with almost every Charm having some Elemental interaction.<br /> <br /> I think the major issue here is the fact that Intimacies are the 'working parts' of the Social Interaction System. I feel like many in this thread who want to shorten the mentioned 4-step system are moving in the direction (knowingly or not) of a 'skill roll resolution' social system, which is explicitly not what Exalted is. Using an analog to Exalted's combat system, wanting to 'automatically create' Intimacies you can then exploit is akin to wanting to be able to just gain Initiative so you can make more Decisive Attacks, ideally without having to make Withering Attacks at all. That just isn't how the system works.<br /> <br /> Now, someone who wants to be very good--and self-sufficiently so--at Social combat simply cannot ignore Socialize. Under the social system, knowledge (of intimacies) is power. And Socialize does double duty as both gaining knowledge of others and hiding knowledge of self. It is very much the Melee of Social combat. People who ignore it just... I mean, I feel that that can't really understand the social interaction system if they think they can be 'a social expert' and not have it.<br /> <br /> I can't help feeling that someone who wants to be able to generate intimacies on demand doesn't really understand the system. It feels very much like, 'I don't really care what this guy thinks; I just want him to do what I want.' I mean, how different is this, really, from overt mind control?<br /> <br /> For myself, this feels like people wanting to drive a bulldozer through a Zen rock garden. The social interaction system lends itself to indirection, wheeling, and dealing. It is not this 'hit this guy over the head with my great idea until he caves' type of approach. My approach to social situations in Exalted 3E works like this:<br /> <br /> Step 1) Determine your goal and identify your target.<br /> Step 2) Gain as much information about the target's Intimacies (and others' Intimacies affiliated with the target) as possible while hiding your own. Primary Ability: Socialize<br /> Step 3) Start Instilling Intimacies that are potentially supportive of your goal. Primary Ability: Presence or possibly Performance. NB: This is the primary location for draining your target's Willpower.<br /> Step 4) Once the target's social situation (Intimacies and remaining Willpower) are sufficient, Persuade. Ideally, the target is low on Willpower and/or has a very difficult time resisting your influence.<br /> <br /> This is the basic game plan. Note that Step 3) is the most optional, in some ways. If the target's Intimacy array greatly supports your goal already, Instilling <i>may</i> not be necessary. It can still be useful to drain Willpower, though. Ideally, your target should not know your goal until the Persuade hits. Well, <i>ideally</i>, your target should not know your goal even after the Persuasion. But you get the idea.<br /> <br /> I feel that there also needs to be an obligatory reminder to STs that providing their NPCs with few if any Intimacies and/or having them spend WP all the time is not really playing fairly. I view it as the Social analog to fudging numbers so PCs miss in combat, etc. The social system is quite rich, and while the 'hard pass' of WP can be annoying (and tempting), I have not seen any other system that does better to capture the dynamics.<br /> <br /> So... I don't know. I do hope that the ST book coming covers issues like these in a lot greater detail.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3551-ulthwithian","name":"Ulthwithian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T09:58:43-08:00","id":1287978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulthwithian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286718-solar-presence-versus-dragon-blooded-presence?p=1287942#post1287942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the basic game plan. Note that Step 3) is the most optional, in some ways. If the target's Intimacy array greatly supports your goal already, Instilling <i>may</i> not be necessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe I\u2019m just too generous of a ST but even this seems wrong to me. When attempting a persuade action you don\u2019t actually need to be targeting an intimacy that directly supports the action, I mean if you are then great, but it\u2019s wholly unneeded. Like if you\u2019re talking to a local town leader and she\u2019s got these intimacies:<br /> <br /> Defining - I revere my ancestors<br /> Defining - Husband (love)<br /> <br /> Major - I am the rightful ruler of these people<br /> Major - Swaying Spider (fear)<br /> <br /> Minor - When it rains, it pours.<br /> <br /> <br /> And lets say you know all these, or at least a few, from your investigations or socialize. Now you\u2019re trying to convince her to join up and fight the Realm. You don\u2019t need to go through instilling a defining intimacy of hatred for the Realm. I mean you might want to just to make her even more devoted to the cause, but it\u2019s not required at all. All you need to do is say \u201cYour ancestors shed blood, sweat, and tears. Their own and their foes to protect this land, and you\u2019d give it up to some foreigners without a fight?\u201d What you\u2019ve done there is target her ancestors intimacy to lever the action you want her to take. What she might do is bring her love of her husband up as a reason why she shouldn\u2019t, bolstering her resolve with a defining intimacy and arguing that she doesn\u2019t want to see him hurt in war. If you exceed her Resolve even then, which as a Solar you will, then she has no third intimacy of defining level to bring her to a decision point, she doesn\u2019t even have the option to spend a willpower, she is compelled to declare war.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T10:55:03-08:00","id":1287997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286718-solar-presence-versus-dragon-blooded-presence?p=1287978#post1287978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe I\u2019m just too generous of a ST but even this seems wrong to me. When attempting a persuade action you don\u2019t actually need to be targeting an intimacy that directly supports the action, I mean if you are then great, but it\u2019s wholly unneeded. Like if you\u2019re talking to a local town leader and she\u2019s got these intimacies:<br /> <br /> Defining - I revere my ancestors<br /> Defining - Husband (love)<br /> <br /> Major - I am the rightful ruler of these people<br /> Major - Swaying Spider (fear)<br /> <br /> Minor - When it rains, it pours.<br /> <br /> <br /> And lets say you know all these, or at least a few, from your investigations or socialize. Now you\u2019re trying to convince her to join up and fight the Realm. You don\u2019t need to go through instilling a defining intimacy of hatred for the Realm. I mean you might want to just to make her even more devoted to the cause, but it\u2019s not required at all. All you need to do is say \u201cYour ancestors shed blood, sweat, and tears. Their own and their foes to protect this land, and you\u2019d give it up to some foreigners without a fight?\u201d What you\u2019ve done there is target her ancestors intimacy to lever the action you want her to take. What she might do is bring her love of her husband up as a reason why she shouldn\u2019t, bolstering her resolve with a defining intimacy and arguing that she doesn\u2019t want to see him hurt in war. If you exceed her Resolve even then, which as a Solar you will, then she has no third intimacy of defining level to bring her to a decision point, she doesn\u2019t even have the option to spend a willpower, she is compelled to declare war.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're entirely correct, here. I'm just saying that there are lots of moving pieces in the social system, and there are many ways to an end short of instituting house rules that blatantly favor Solars.<br /> <br /> It generally does require more work than combat on the part of the player. If one of my players would say, &quot;I exploit this intimacy of theirs,&quot; my immediate response is, 'How?' unless it's blatantly obvious. I just feel that many players (and possibly STs) believe that Intimacies are overly narrow. I know many people who would believe there is no possible way to have 'I revere my ancestors' to support 'fight the Realm', as one example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3551-ulthwithian","name":"Ulthwithian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T12:19:37-08:00","id":1288027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulthwithian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286718-solar-presence-versus-dragon-blooded-presence?p=1287997#post1287997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you're entirely correct, here. I'm just saying that there are lots of moving pieces in the social system, and there are many ways to an end short of instituting house rules that blatantly favor Solars.<br /> <br /> It generally does require more work than combat on the part of the player. If one of my players would say, &amp;quot;I exploit this intimacy of theirs,&amp;quot; my immediate response is, 'How?' unless it's blatantly obvious. I just feel that many players (and possibly STs) believe that Intimacies are overly narrow. I know many people who would believe there is no possible way to have 'I revere my ancestors' to support 'fight the Realm', as one example.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that makes it harder than it needs to be. I can also see it the other way too, if you\u2019re a Dynast who\u2019s trying to stop a rebellion you could easily say: <br /> <br /> \u201cThe Realm is the greatest power in the world, and I know the general assigned to this area personally. She gives no quarter and has a penchant for destroying architecture. I really don\u2019t like her much personally, but we both have to deal with her. Think of all your ancestors gave birth to, these sacred halls, the great paintings, even you and your lineage. Don\u2019t let that be destroyed in a futile struggle, protect what they poured their hearts and souls into, save it for your own children to witness. Keep peace, your lives and your art are too beautiful to be burned to ash in her ambitions.\u201d<br /> <br /> That\u2019s ALSO exploiting their ancestor reverence, to do completely the opposite thing. A little good-cop bad-cop routine. The key is how convincing are you that the way to revere their ancestors is to not go to war. Especially considering a Solar strongman can tear a castle tower from its foundations, a Solar duelist can parry a falling mountain, a Solar loremaster can predict the doom of an entire nation by prophecy, it seems weird that people put so many restrictions on a solar diplomat to convince people.<br /> <br /> The persuade system that we have in place, thank GOD, is just there to stop some dick from rolling 30 successes and convincing Cathak Cainen to give you his armies and betray the Realm, tell Pelops Deled to stop worrying and love anathema, and then tell Mnemon that she looks fat and should give you control of her entire house while she goes on a diet. None of those things are really epic they\u2019re just dumb. On the other hand I can see all three of those things, Cathak siding with you in a war, redeeming the master of the Hunt, and getting Mnemon to step down from power, being cool climaxes after a campaign of epic social interactions. That\u2019s the Zenith/Eclipse version of slaying The Ebon Dragon in mortal combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-03T20:48:04-08:00","id":1293650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286718-solar-presence-versus-dragon-blooded-presence?p=1286769#post1286769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Essentially, Solar Presence charms do four main things well:<br /> <br /> Buff your friends<br /> Help you get lots of successes for cheap<br /> Help you intimidate people<br /> Help you seduce people<br /> <br /> None of those let you deal with the difficulty of persuading people to take significant actions when they don't already have a Major intimacy. And if they already did have a Major intimacy? There's a decent chance you wouldn't need to Persuade them anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about Bargain actions? Like Threaten actions, they bypass the Intimacy requirements of Persuade actions. It's not as convenient as getting them to agree to do something for essentially nothing, but causes fewer complications than Threatening them to do something lest you hurt them.<br /> <br /> <br /> Right off the bat, the Solar Presence Excellency is vital to Bargain actions.<br /> <br /> Harmonious Presence Meditation and Awakened Carnal Demiurge will help, but the middle point between them, Threefold Magnetic Ardor, excludes Bargain actions from its assistance.<br /> <br /> Enemy-Castigating Solar Judgment would help you Bargain with creatures of darkness.<br /> <br /> Fulminating Word specifically includes Bargain actions among the social influence it may supplement.<br /> <br /> Crowned King of Eternity helps.<br /> <br /> (Huh. What is Worshipful Lackey Acquisition doing in Presence when it requires a Performance action to function?)<br /> <br /> <br /> But for toothier Bargain-oriented Charms, Solars might need to look to Bureaucracy.<br /> <br /> Frugal Merchant Method and Insightful Buyer Technique help you determine how valuable items are in your target's market of choice.<br /> <br /> Deft Official's Way can point you to the best person to bargain with, which may not be the person you thought you needed to influence.<br /> <br /> Enlightened Discourse Method and Semantic Argument Technique are just more dice-adders. Not sure how much you need that if you're using Solar Presence.<br /> <br /> Irresistible Salesman Spirit lets you double 7s on a Bargain action (no dice-limit concerns here), which Solar Presence definitely doesn't do.<br /> <br /> It also doesn't have anything like Soul-Snaring Pitch, which is a persuade action that lets you set up a bargain action by convincing someone that a Trivial reward is worth agreeing to perform a Life-Defining Task. Of course, you do run into the usual limitations of persuade actions and Intimacies, so maybe that doesn't actually bypass any of the problems players are having with Solar Presence. At least having Listener-Swaying Argument and Impassioned Discourse Technique helps ram this one through.<br /> <br /> Subject-Hailing Ideology helps get around Intimacies by letting you treat former or eroded Intimacies as though they were at their former strength, under a particular condition.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Terrestrial Bureaucracy Excellency can't help your Presence-based bargain actions with that sweet, sweet &quot;re-roll all 6s&quot; effect. Instead, you can enjoy the Terrestrial Presence Excellency's benefit of adding an additional non-Charm die for every 10 you roll.<br /> <br /> But at least Terrestrial Bureaucracy in general perhaps gets to the heart of the matter sooner with Finding the Water's Depths, to help you figure out what your specific target might specifically want in return for performing the specific task you want of them.<br /> <br /> Shells-for-Silver Ruse lets you deceive your mark about your exact level of wealth, and leverage that lie as a Minor Intimacy.<br /> <br /> Thoughtful Gift Technique builds upon Finding the Water's Depths, avoiding dice-adding limitations by doubling 9s.<br /> <br /> The Water Signature Charm, Distraction of the Babbling Brook, lets you bypass certain Intimacies in the target with a bargain where they unwittingly agree to more than they think, but you're probably going to want to throw Finding the Water's Depths and Thoughtful Gift Technique behind that dice-roll.<br /> <br /> Drowning In Negotiation helps enforce any bargain, including onerous ones imposed with Distraction of the Babbling Brook.<br /> <br /> The Wood Signature Charm of One Forest, Many Trees might allow you to get what you want without needing to persuade or bargain with anyone, if what you want can be gained through this Charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-03T22:25:49-08:00","id":1293665,"title":"","content":"For whatever reson, the previous devs didn't think there shit out. So what you have is solars throwing 25 dice and getting stopped. Unfortunately, you cannot combine this with new mechanics that things like lunars show. You need to get rid of a number of the dice tricks to balance it out. <br /> <br /> Solars are cursed with being first in a newly designed system a lot of their tools are going to be archic and yet incompatible without severe ovehauls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-03T22:53:06-08:00","id":1293668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286718-solar-presence-versus-dragon-blooded-presence?p=1293665#post1293665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what you have is solars throwing 25 dice and getting stopped.</div> </div> </div> </div>To what are you referring?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-03T23:14:28-08:00","id":1293669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286718-solar-presence-versus-dragon-blooded-presence?p=1293668#post1293668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To what are you referring?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think he's referring to a willpower expenditure being able to stop a new intimacy from being formed, or a major/defining intimacy being weakened. No matter how many dice you have somebody can just do that, and really antagonistic STs might take that to mean do it at literally any opportunity. <br /> <br /> I get why they're there though, so you can't have an afternoon of conversation with Mnemon and convert her to the cult of the illuminated, but at the same time it does protect the PCs from having that happen to them too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-03T23:42:48-08:00","id":1293677,"title":"","content":"I'd hate to have a killer ST that abuses the system by having people spend WP at the drop of the hat despite the book saying its something people don't do a lot IC because its supposed to represent a huge taxing effort. Its like having one who responds to you pushing through a crowd by declaring that you have to roll combat because now everyone in the crowd has whipped out knives and are trying to kill you for the slight against their honor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T04:43:48-08:00","id":1293696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286718-solar-presence-versus-dragon-blooded-presence?p=1293677#post1293677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd hate to have a killer ST that abuses the system by having people spend WP at the drop of the hat despite the book saying its something people don't do a lot IC because its supposed to represent a huge taxing effort. Its like having one who responds to you pushing through a crowd by declaring that you have to roll combat because now everyone in the crowd has whipped out knives and are trying to kill you for the slight against their honor.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not really the faceless peon who matters. Almost all the major antagonists in the game would block it. The problem is that presence lets you run through everything so it has the defence of willpower. A solar targetting intimacies can get pretty far with the willpower drain already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T07:43:45-08:00","id":1293748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286718-solar-presence-versus-dragon-blooded-presence?p=1293696#post1293696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not really the faceless peon who matters. Almost all the major antagonists in the game would block it. The problem is that presence lets you run through everything so it has the defence of willpower. A solar targetting intimacies can get pretty far with the willpower drain already.</div> </div> </div> </div>The willpower can\u2019t defend against everything though, if the presence Solar, using a persuade action, targets a defining intimacy that their target has, there\u2019s almost nothing they can do to stop it. They\u2019d need another 2 defining intimacies that oppose the action. <br /> <br /> Like if you wanted to convince Berit to betray the Realm based on her own pride, you could target her pride, she\u2019d bring her loyalty to the Realm up to help defend, but you\u2019re a Solar so who cares, and then she\u2019s is left with nothing to bring about a descision point when she fails. <br /> <br /> Now, admittedly that limits you to actions that you can justify targeting her pride for, but maybe you can work up her minor tie of \u201cthe battlefield is where I belong\u201d to defining, because willpower can\u2019t stop that, and that gives you more options. I think Solars probably have the worst designed charmset in the game right now, but it isn\u2019t totally awful. Their ability to succeed at any social roll means that as long as you\u2019re playing by the rules of the social system you can do pretty much anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T08:26:40-08:00","id":1293761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286718-solar-presence-versus-dragon-blooded-presence?p=1293696#post1293696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not really the faceless peon who matters. Almost all the major antagonists in the game would block it. The problem is that presence lets you run through everything so it has the defence of willpower. A solar targetting intimacies can get pretty far with the willpower drain already.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its advice was that even <i>important</i> characters aren't likely to make the massive amount of effort required in spending WP unless you are stepping on the toes of a higher intimacy or they have really good not intimacy reason to not want to do what you are suggesting like 'my liege the Mask of Winters would kill me and soul forge my ghost into an ash tray if I betray him like that'. The sidebar in question is on page 220 of the core if you want to check it out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T08:28:38-08:00","id":1293764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286718-solar-presence-versus-dragon-blooded-presence?p=1293748#post1293748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The willpower can\u2019t defend against everything though, if the presence Solar, using a persuade action, targets a defining intimacy that their target has, there\u2019s almost nothing they can do to stop it. They\u2019d need another 2 defining intimacies that oppose the action.<br /> <br /> Like if you wanted to convince Berit to betray the Realm based on her own pride, you could target her pride, she\u2019d bring her loyalty to the Realm up to help defend, but you\u2019re a Solar so who cares, and then she\u2019s is left with nothing to bring about a descision point when she fails.<br /> <br /> Now, admittedly that limits you to actions that you can justify targeting her pride for, but maybe you can work up her minor tie of \u201cthe battlefield is where I belong\u201d to defining, because willpower can\u2019t stop that, and that gives you more options. I think Solars probably have the worst designed charmset in the game right now, but it isn\u2019t totally awful. Their ability to succeed at any social roll means that as long as you\u2019re playing by the rules of the social system you can do pretty much anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>As someone who's just reread the influence system, that's going to bounce hard as an unacceptable order. You can use her pride to get her to do some things, but any major betrayal of the Realm, like allying with solars to help take the empire over or bring it down, isn't going to fly.<br /> <br /> More interestingly to me is how often do players get hit with social influence from NPCs? If PCs are the only one dishing it out, then that's a bit like using the combat system but only players get to make attacks. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5001-soul_porpoise","name":"soul_porpoise","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T08:35:14-08:00","id":1293768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>soul_porpoise</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286718-solar-presence-versus-dragon-blooded-presence?p=1293764#post1293764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As someone who's just reread the influence system, that's going to bounce hard as an unacceptable order. You can use her pride to get her to do some things, but any major betrayal of the Realm, like allying with solars to help take the empire over or bring it down, isn't going to fly.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>As someone who hasn't, can you explain why it would be an unacceptable order? I thought that was just about suicide and such.<br /> <br /> On a side note how does the system deal with something that seems minor (just let someone in through the side gate during the night) but the character suspect may be for more serious (that person might be on their way to assassinate the Empress), especially if there's not been any read intentions rolls or such in the meantime? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25050-fodor","name":"FODOR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T08:36:28-08:00","id":1293770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286718-solar-presence-versus-dragon-blooded-presence?p=1293696#post1293696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Almost all the major antagonists in the game would block it.</div> </div> </div> </div>What a tremendously dull way to play through the process of social interactions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T08:46:34-08:00","id":1293776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286718-solar-presence-versus-dragon-blooded-presence?p=1293696#post1293696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is that presence lets you run through everything so it has the defence of willpower.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, not Persuade actions when they don't have an applicable intimacy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A solar targetting intimacies can get pretty far with the willpower drain already. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but if you know their intimacies, and they have an intimacy that supports it (and is strong enough), then you're getting them to do something that's not really far out of their mindset anyway.<br /> <br /> I think the main defence against, say, murdering someone, is having no motive for killing someone. (And, tbh, something like that's going to have to be Major or even Defining.) Your intimacy of &quot;murder is wrong&quot; is really just the second defence. Willpower's like third.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T08:56:37-08:00","id":1293782,"title":"","content":"This just makes me think more about the ton of Lunar charms that prevent you from spending Willpower or cut off intimacies for you to apply for defense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T08:59:03-08:00","id":1293784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286718-solar-presence-versus-dragon-blooded-presence?p=1293770#post1293770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What a tremendously dull way to play through the process of social interactions.</div> </div> </div> </div>It won't always happen but it depends what you want to happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T09:12:19-08:00","id":1293786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286718-solar-presence-versus-dragon-blooded-presence?p=1293782#post1293782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This just makes me think more about the ton of Lunar charms that prevent you from spending Willpower or cut off intimacies for you to apply for defense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yet what they don't do is combine it with a whole bunch of cheap dice and success adders.<br /> <br /> For Solars who've invested in Presence charms, blowing past the enemies Resolve is easy, but you've still essentially got to convince them the way a human would.<br /> <br /> For Lunars (and, to some extent, Dragonblood), there are various ways you can confuse your enemy so they don't apply everything, making things like Persuade, Intimidate, Bargain, Seduce, easier than for a human (bargain with trash, persuade people who hate you, intimidate without making people angry). But rolling against a character with high Integrity and some defensive intimacies is actually pretty hard.<br /> <br /> I'm not 100% sure if this is a deliberate dichotomy, or an evolution in charm design.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T09:20:43-08:00","id":1293791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286718-solar-presence-versus-dragon-blooded-presence?p=1293786#post1293786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yet what they don't do is combine it with a whole bunch of cheap dice and success adders.<br /> <br /> For Solars who've invested in Presence charms, blowing past the enemies Resolve is easy, but you've still essentially got to convince them the way a human would.<br /> <br /> For Lunars (and, to some extent, Dragonblood), there are various ways you can confuse your enemy so they don't apply everything, making things like Persuade, Intimidate, Bargain, Seduce, easier than for a human (bargain with trash, persuade people who hate you, intimidate without making people angry). But rolling against a character with high Integrity and some defensive intimacies is actually pretty hard.<br /> <br /> I'm not 100% sure if this is a deliberate dichotomy, or an evolution in charm design.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is an interesting examination that soothes me a bit with some of how powerful Lunar social abilities seem to be. I suppose it's easy to just assume someone can break through your Resolve when you're used to just Solars, and are viewing everyone as having the base Solar ability to explode Resolves easily.<br /> <br /> Lunars do have a pretty good charm in that they can make a powerful intimacy apply as a penalty instead, but I suppose that may be countered out by a different powerful intimacy, then it's just a roll off, particularly between Exalts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T09:38:31-08:00","id":1293799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286718-solar-presence-versus-dragon-blooded-presence?p=1293782#post1293782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This just makes me think more about the ton of Lunar charms that prevent you from spending Willpower or cut off intimacies for you to apply for defense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunar social Charms also tend to be flexible about whether they enhance a persuade or bargain action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 03-04-2019, 12:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T09:46:09-08:00","id":1293804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>soul_porpoise</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286718-solar-presence-versus-dragon-blooded-presence?p=1293764#post1293764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As someone who's just reread the influence system, that's going to bounce hard as an unacceptable order. You can use her pride to get her to do some things, but any major betrayal of the Realm, like allying with solars to help take the empire over or bring it down, isn't going to fly.<br /> <br /> More interestingly to me is how often do players get hit with social influence from NPCs? If PCs are the only one dishing it out, then that's a bit like using the combat system but only players get to make attacks. </div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yes, betray the Realm as in cast everything aside and join the anathema then yes, that\u2019s unacceptable. Consider this though, Berit was never given a house, perhaps that\u2019s because, eventually, the Empress saw her as the only true successor. The one who would have to rise above house politics and this could not have one herself. The Realm needs that leadership now, but it\u2019s poised on the edge of a destructive conflict that will tear it apart. The only real option to come out of this strong is for one side to win a decisive victory now so they can re-form a unified front against the enemies of the Dynasty, maybe even reunified under Berit\u2019s rule at last. Now I roll persuade to get her to give up her knowledge of the defences in the Eagle prefecture under the pretence that house V\u2019Neef must be crushed first to ensure Berit\u2019s only other rival is Mnemon. Except way more convincing than that because I\u2019m not a demigod.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T09:53:52-08:00","id":1293808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286718-solar-presence-versus-dragon-blooded-presence?p=1293791#post1293791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is an interesting examination that soothes me a bit with some of how powerful Lunar social abilities seem to be. I suppose it's easy to just assume someone can break through your Resolve when you're used to just Solars, and are viewing everyone as having the base Solar ability to explode Resolves easily.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, +4 Resolve for a Defining Intimacy is, frankly, enormous. That's equivalent to 8 dice.<br /> Obviously you can blow through mortals Resolve with an excellency, but blowing through the Resolve of a Sidereal or Abyssal or Dragonblood with Integrity charms is a very different matter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lunars do have a pretty good charm in that they can make a powerful intimacy apply as a penalty instead, but I suppose that may be countered out by a different powerful intimacy, then it's just a roll off, particularly between Exalts. </div> </div> </div>Which one is that?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T10:01:38-08:00","id":1293811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286718-solar-presence-versus-dragon-blooded-presence?p=1293808#post1293808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, +4 Resolve for a Defining Intimacy is, frankly, enormous. That's equivalent to 8 dice.<br /> Obviously you can blow through mortals Resolve with an excellency, but blowing through the Resolve of a Sidereal or Abyssal or Dragonblood with Integrity charms is a very different matter.<br /> <br /> <br /> Which one is that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Cobra's Hypnotic Gaze and Shadow Faith Inversion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T10:04:34-08:00","id":1293812,"title":"","content":"Ah yeah, those are good.<br /> <br /> Though Shadow Faith Inversion costs a wp and is once/story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T10:06:17-08:00","id":1293813,"title":"","content":"They are both Psyche as well though, so they are clearly supposed to represent a Lunar basically brainwashing you in the same was as Hypnotic Tongue technique is.<br /> <br /> Do DBs even have a Psyche charm at all?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T10:14:05-08:00","id":1293816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286718-solar-presence-versus-dragon-blooded-presence?p=1293813#post1293813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are both Psyche as well though, so they are clearly supposed to represent a Lunar basically brainwashing you in the same was as Hypnotic Tongue technique is.<br /> <br /> Do DBs even have a Psyche charm at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah a bunch actually, usually water aspect. Psyche effects aren\u2019t more powerful though, they\u2019re just using a form of mind manipulation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T10:24:58-08:00","id":1293820,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the Psyche keyword seems to be pulling from late 2E fandom insistence that using any motes at all on your social rolls meant you were literally brainwashing people into doing what you wanted, rather then just being really good at convincing people. So the keyword means charms that really are 'No, actually, this is brain washing and magical manipulation in a negative contex'.<br /> <br /> Or something like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T10:51:04-08:00","id":1293827,"title":"","content":"Well, Solars do have some charms which give out intimacies, up to Defining actually! There is Celestial Bliss Trick obviously, but yeah, that one is... questionable.<br /> <br /> Fortunately there <i>probably </i>are others!<br /> <br /> There is Flowing Mind Prana in Lore for example. Teaching people gives them your intimacies, up to defining, no option of saying no, can't be degraded until they perform a task for you. Of course, how this interacts with npc's is unclear. They don't use xp, you see, and it's 1 intimacy at minor, or an upgrade, per 3 xp granted, but hey. Lets assume it works, yes?<br /> <br /> In Presence there is Worshipful Lackey Acquisition. After achieving a goal through lecture and a bunch of other possible things enemies must roll wits + integrity minus your essence vs your highest social attribute. Appearance can potentially go up to 8. If they don't make it they get a Principle defining them as your acolyte.<br /> <br /> The wording and intent behind this one is even <i>worse</i> than Flowing Mind Prana, Bloody stupid natural language! For starters, it states enemies, but I guess it works on non-enemies too, right? I mean, that restriction makes no sense whatsoever if taken literally, so let's not. Second, <i>a Principle defining them as your acolyte. </i>Oh boy. Could they have been any less clear? Still, they must mean a Defining Principle, because frankly, what else could be saying with that sentence? I don't think it's possible to resist, but that's just a guess, and it also refers to this effect ending, but it's a permanent charm.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, here's one more vote for the Solar Charmset being really shoddily written! That said, I strongly suspect they can give out intimacies!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1550-angwe","name":"Angwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T11:21:47-08:00","id":1293833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Angwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286718-solar-presence-versus-dragon-blooded-presence?p=1293827#post1293827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Presence there is Worshipful Lackey Acquisition. After achieving a goal through lecture and a bunch of other possible things</div> </div> </div> </div>All of which read as Performance actions, which makes it really odd as a Presence Charm.<br /> <br /> Also, the Corebook isn't poorly written so much as &quot;rushed through the playtest phase after some asshole leaked the documents&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T11:34:10-08:00","id":1293834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286718-solar-presence-versus-dragon-blooded-presence?p=1293833#post1293833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All of which read as Performance actions, which makes it really odd as a Presence Charm.<br /> <br /> Also, the Corebook isn't poorly written so much as &amp;quot;rushed through the playtest phase after some asshole leaked the documents&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I really don't want to get into this shit in a thread unrelated to it, but that's really disingenuous to how the core book was made, what happened leading up to the release, and the actions of the old devs.<br /> <br /> There was a leaker, but the fact that even mattered was entirely on the hands of the developers, and their reaction and the result of how the corebook turned out in some issues like clarity and word choice was not entirely the fault of the leaker.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T12:32:40-08:00","id":1293853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Angwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286718-solar-presence-versus-dragon-blooded-presence?p=1293827#post1293827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, Solars do have some charms which give out intimacies, up to Defining actually! There is Celestial Bliss Trick obviously, but yeah, that one is... questionable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or treat someone as though they <i>have</i> a particular intimacy, such as Mastery of Small Manners.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T13:15:25-08:00","id":1293872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286718-solar-presence-versus-dragon-blooded-presence?p=1293833#post1293833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All of which read as Performance actions, which makes it really odd as a Presence Charm.<br /> <br /> Also, the Corebook isn't poorly written so much as &quot;rushed through the playtest phase after some asshole leaked the documents&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering how damned long they took writing it I don't think its fair to say anything about it was 'rushed' as an excuse for poor charm wording.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T15:40:58-08:00","id":1293903,"title":"","content":"Myeah, whatever the reason, it took a long time, a <i>really</i> long time to publish the core, and yes, it still looks rushed and poorly worded, and a shocking amount of Charms seem to reference a previous iteration of the rules set. It is what it is, and at this point we just need to deal with it. Still, even if I were to buy that it the leak bears some responsibility for this, which I do not, it was a conscious design choice to go for natural, inexact language. Lets just say that in my personal opinion that was a mistake.<br /> <br /> The exact (rather unhelpful) wording of 'Worshipful Lackey Acquisition': 'Whenever the Solar achieves a goal through lecture, prophecy, oration, or other forms of performance'. I personally believe, despite the 'other forms of performance', it would trigger of a rather broad set of particular abilities. Definitely Presence, being an essence 3 Presence charm, but also Lore and Performance. The fact that we need to discuss this is pretty annoying, actually, and very avoidable really! I also hate the 'enemies' and 'those who conspire against her' parts. Is that fluff or mechanics? Is it really only expected not to work on those who are actually inclined, or at the very least not opposed to follow the Solar in the first place? Actually, what <i>are </i>enemies? And really, would have been so hard to put in clear mechanical terms the level of intimacy it bestows instead of strongly implying? And what's this talk of when the effect ends in a permanent charm? Aaaaaargh... And is Flowing Mind Prana only supposed to work on the other PC's, because no one else uses xp? That can't be the intent!<br /> <br /> Anyway, people were saying Solars couldn't just bypass the instill part and go straight to handing out intimacies. They can, they <i>definitely</i> can, and better than the rest. The Charms may be unclear, or some of them, Mastery of Small Manners is pretty straightforward if only a minor intimacy, but as demonstrated, there are some which hand out Defining intimacies, even if we are left guessing when, how and to whom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1550,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1550-angwe","user":"Angwe","date":". 03-04-2019, 06:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1550-angwe","name":"Angwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T16:01:01-08:00","id":1293909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286718-solar-presence-versus-dragon-blooded-presence?p=1293808#post1293808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, +4 Resolve for a Defining Intimacy is, frankly, enormous. That's equivalent to 8 dice.<br /> Obviously you can blow through mortals Resolve with an excellency, but blowing through the Resolve of a Sidereal or Abyssal or Dragonblood with Integrity charms is a very different matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>We'd have to wait to see those charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T17:12:06-08:00","id":1293921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286718-solar-presence-versus-dragon-blooded-presence?p=1293909#post1293909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We'd have to wait to see those charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>We <i>have</i> Dragon-Blooded Integrity Charms already, and everything we've heard about Abyssals so far doesn't suggest their ability to bolster Resolve will be particularly subpar compared to their Solar brethren. The only one we should feel unsure about, is Sidereals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 03-04-2019, 08:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T22:19:02-08:00","id":1293965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286718-solar-presence-versus-dragon-blooded-presence?p=1293786#post1293786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not 100% sure if this is a deliberate dichotomy, or an evolution in charm design.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m 99% sure it\u2019s the latter, and that it\u2019s specifically a matter of Vance and Minton having fewer reservations than Holden and Morke about subverting the social influence system\u2019s \u201csafeguards.\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T22:42:09-08:00","id":1293967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286718-solar-presence-versus-dragon-blooded-presence?p=1293909#post1293909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We'd have to wait to see those charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but we know a DB can get to Resolve 14 with an excellency and intimacy. That's without charm purchases. And that's not easy to get through.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T22:50:02-08:00","id":1293970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286718-solar-presence-versus-dragon-blooded-presence?p=1293965#post1293965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019m 99% sure it\u2019s the latter, and that it\u2019s specifically a matter of Vance and Minton having fewer reservations than Holden and Morke about subverting the social influence system\u2019s \u201csafeguards.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not <i>usually </i>a good thing, see 2e's Epic Zeal of (Virtue), I think it works in this case though because it actually does kind of fit with the Solar style. It's why they don't get a charm like Soaring Zephyr Flight. Eagle Wing Style is actually a better charm for almost anything you'd care to use it for, but it isn't just straight up flight in the same way at all. It helps that the DB ones especially have their own safeguards built in, even if they subvert the normal ones.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286718-solar-presence-versus-dragon-blooded-presence?p=1293967#post1293967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure, but we know a DB can get to Resolve 14 with an excellency and intimacy. That's without charm purchases. And that's not easy to get through.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, what, how does a DB get to 14 with just an excellency and an intimacy? Are you counting stunts/willpower?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T23:17:10-08:00","id":1293974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286718-solar-presence-versus-dragon-blooded-presence?p=1293965#post1293965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019m 99% sure it\u2019s the latter, and that it\u2019s specifically a matter of Vance and Minton having fewer reservations than Holden and Morke about subverting the social influence system\u2019s \u201csafeguards.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>Ask them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T23:59:07-08:00","id":1293977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286718-solar-presence-versus-dragon-blooded-presence?p=1293970#post1293970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not <i>usually </i>a good thing, see 2e's Epic Zeal of (Virtue), I think it works in this case though because it actually does kind of fit with the Solar style. It's why they don't get a charm like Soaring Zephyr Flight. Eagle Wing Style is actually a better charm for almost anything you'd care to use it for, but it isn't just straight up flight in the same way at all. It helps that the DB ones especially have their own safeguards built in, even if they subvert the normal ones.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Wait, what, how does a DB get to 14 with just an excellency and an intimacy? Are you counting stunts/willpower?</div> </div> </div> </div>1pt stunts, yeah.<br /> Resolve 6, +3 excellency, +4 intimacy, +1 stunt.<br /> <br /> This requires an applicable speciality though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T00:14:01-08:00","id":1293978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286718-solar-presence-versus-dragon-blooded-presence?p=1293977#post1293977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1pt stunts, yeah.<br /> Resolve 6, +3 excellency, +4 intimacy, +1 stunt.<br /> <br /> This requires an applicable speciality though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh right, that's true, although if you're ta